WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.153 --> 00:00:01.450
(dramatic piano music)

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:04.530
- [Ahmad] Every time I
dance, I try to do my best

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:08.090
and I give the most because
living in the war taught me

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.150
maybe this time, it will
be the last dance for you.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.630
Maybe you will be killed in a bomb

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.240
or a bullet or something
when you leave the studio.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.250
So every time I would give my best

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.650
and live it to the most.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.310
- [Narrator] Ahmad Joudeh
was born in the Yarmouk Camp,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.810
a refugee camp for Palestinians in Syria.

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.150
Despite his tumultuous surroundings,

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.920
he found escape in a hobby
uncommon in his culture.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.420
- I saw dance for the first time

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.520
when I was a child-8 years old,

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.530
'cause I was fascinated by their movements

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.673
and by the music that they are moving on.

00:00:51.673 --> 00:00:54.860
I learned how to dance
through videos on YouTube,

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.070
and I was doing this every
day in my room secretly

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:03.380
because dancing in my
culture, especially for a man,

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.083
it's something to be ashamed of.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.590
My life was in danger when I was in Syria

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:10.430
because I was a dancer

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:14.690
and that's because of the extremist people

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.320
who came into our country

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.050
and then I start to
receive all these messages

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.970
or phone calls or those kind of things

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.390
that telling me they want to cut my head,

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:27.767
and that's why I had my
tattoo dance or die on my neck

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:30.800
'cause I carry my life on my neck.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.910
And if they would've killed me,

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:36.010
I wanted it to be the last
thing they can see from me,

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.323
so it's dance or die.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.540
- [Narrator] While in Syria,

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.400
Ahmad went on to receive
formal dance training

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.482
and would post videos of his dancing

00:01:49.482 --> 00:01:52.830
and was eventually discovered
by a documentary filmmaker

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:56.010
from Holland who wanted to tell his story.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.480
The film was seen by the
Dutch National Ballet,

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.300
who offered him a scholarship.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.197
He has since gone on to
perform all over Europe.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.170
- We are here in Kilden Theater

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.270
talking about social media.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.270
In this production, I'm acting myself

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:15.360
because social media played
the most important role

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.470
in saving my life in my story;

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.390
because through social media, I was seen

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.053
and I was rescued.

00:02:25.781 --> 00:02:27.820
(playful orchestral music)

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.500
What made me keep dancing

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.610
and keep on doing what am
I doing even 'til today

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.690
because I believe the
artist has the same duty

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:40.230
like the soldier to fight for his country

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.350
and the artist can fight for culture

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:44.590
and for art and for history.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:47.240
And if we don't have art and
culture in our countries,

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.120
what are we fighting for?

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.260
Away from dance, I am
nothing, and I have nothing.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:56.403
All I have is dance, and
all I am is the dancer.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.570
Then maybe in the far future,

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.655
sometimes I see myself sitting in a chair

00:03:03.655 --> 00:03:06.950
as an old man in theater in Syria

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:10.410
directing the Syrian National
Ballet that I will find,

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.033
so I hope this dream will come true.

00:03:20.177 --> 00:03:22.927
(tones pinging)

